{"id": "53a114c8-f9ab-40c1-8396-8a9af4fe4b0d", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T15:21:32.049918", "source": "user", "parent_id": "00be620b-32a5-4d9e-bfae-f16420f32418", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Bhai, kaam shuru karne se pehle sirf teen cheezein chahiye — poora solution abhi mat do.\\n\\n1) Input/repository inspection: is repo mein zero-bubble pipeline parallelism ke liye 1F1B, 1F1B-I, ZB-1p aur ZB-2p actually kahan implement hain? Ye cheezein clearly report karo:\\n   - method/scheduler ke naam aur unke entry points (file + symbol), aur ek chhota code-level note ki har method microbatch count ko kaise leta hai (kaunsi config/argument hai),\\n   - koi built-in simulator / cost model hai ya real GPU execution chahiye (runtime, forward/backward durations, bubble calculation),\\n   - throughput kaise nikalne ka convention repo mein already maujood hai (samples/sec, tokens/sec, TFLOPs, iteration time),\\n   - kitne stages (pipeline depth) aur kitne devices default hain, aur koi existing test/example script hai jise harness ke tor par reuse kiya ja sakta hai,\\n   - environment reality: hamare paas GPU nahi hai aur network band hai — batao bina compute ke kitna kaam sirf analytical/simulator level par ho sakta hai.\\n\\n2) Proposed approach (design-only, experiment chalana zaroori nahi): ek short plan do ki experiment design kaise banayenge — kaunsa factor kaunsa level, microbatch count par kaunse values, stages/model-size ka fixed setting, throughput metric ka definition, control variables (jo har method ke liye same rakhne hain taaki comparison fair rahe), aur result ko question se kaise map karenge: teen methods (1F1B, 1F1B-I, ZB-1p) ke liye monotonic improvement check, aur ZB-2p ke liye kam microbatch par bhi high throughput check. Sath mein rationale, controls, analysis plan (kaunsa comparison, kaunsa decision rule ya threshold for \\\"improvement\\\" aur \\\"high throughput\\\") aur feasibility note (GPU na hone par design kis basis par valid rahega) — sab briefly.\\n\\n3) Consequential assumptions / uncertainties: jo bhi cheez repo se confirm nahi hui use \\\"assumption\\\" likho, fact mat batao. Khas taur par: microbatch count ke kaunse discrete values lenge, \\\"high throughput\\\" ka baseline kiske against hai (1F1B relative efficiency), memory constraint ka consideration chahiye ya nahi, aur kya per-step time ya steady-state throughput use hogi (warmup/pehle iteration ko handle kaise karenge).\\n\\nJo cheez repo mein nahi mili use \\\"unknown\\\" bolo, guess mat bharna. Design hi final deliverable hai, isliye inspection aur approach par focus rakho — aur please micromanage mat karo, apni reasoning ke saath do.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the throughput for methods 1F1B, 1F1B-I, and ZB-1p improve as the number of microbatches increases, while ZB-2p maintains high throughput even with fewer microbatches? (Note: These methods are implemented as part of the zero bubble pipeline parallelism strategies in this repository, which aim to reduce pipeline bubbles and maintain high throughput.)\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
